      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/",
      "artist": "Yewenyi at English Wikipedia",
      "description": "Photo taken and supplied by Brian Voon Yee Yap.\nThis steel track was produced by Krupp for a segment of the South Australian Railways.  It is now at the Rail Museum at Adelaide River, Northern Territory and relates to the original Pine Creek Railway running south from Darwin, Northern Territory.\nThe gauge is 3' 6\" (1067mm).\nThe sign in the photo reads as follows:\n\nNorth Australian Railway 1888 to 1976\n\nOriginal Rails\n\nfrom Palmerston to Pine Creek Railway\n\nmarked \"1885 KRUPP P &amp; PC R\"\n\nAs it was a long lead time item, 10,000 (tons?) of this rail was ordered by South\nAustralian Railways in 188_ for supply to the railway contractor.  The rails\nwere made by Krupp at Essen in Germany.\n\nThis section was found one mile south of Adelaide River railway station in October 2001.",
